From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: report release_object(NULL) rather than faulting.

init_directories() passes the result of every create_*() straight to
release_object(), on the assumption that none of them can fail. On this console
some do, and the first anyone hears of it is a null dereference inside
release_object -- which names neither the creation that failed nor any of the
ones after it, because the server is dead.

Report it and return. The startup then continues and every failure is named,
instead of the first being fatal and anonymous.
---
diff --git a/server/object.c b/server/object.c
index e977b89480..ecec88cd0f 100644
--- a/server/object.c
+++ b/server/object.c
@@ -562,6 +562,20 @@ struct object *grab_object( void *ptr )
 /* release an object (i.e. decrement its refcount) */
 void release_object( void *ptr )
 {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. init_directories() passes the result of each create_*()
+     * straight to release_object(), assuming none can fail. On this console
+     * some do, and the null dereference here is the first anyone hears of it --
+     * with no way to tell which creation it was. Name it and carry on, so the
+     * rest of the startup runs and every failure is reported instead of the
+     * first one being fatal and anonymous. */
+    if (!ptr)
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, "wineserver: release_object(NULL) -- a create_* call failed\n" );
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     struct object *obj = (struct object *)ptr;
     assert( obj->refcount );
     if (!--obj->refcount)
